.TH DT-COPY 1 "August 2026" "dirtoo tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dt-copy \- copy files and directories (dirtoo / dirops)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dt-copy
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.I FROM
.I TO
.PP
.B dt-copy
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.B \-t
.I DIR
.I FILE\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Copy files or directory trees. Symbolic links are copied as symbolic links
(not followed). Uses the same
.B dirops
conflict policies as the dirtoo GUI.
.PP
In the two-path form, if
.I TO
is an existing directory, the source basename is placed inside it.
With
.BR \-t ,
each source is copied into
.I DIR
using its basename only.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-target\-directory " " \fIDIR\fR
Multi-source mode: destination directory.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print planned copies; do not write.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print each successful copy.
.TP
.BR \-Y ", " \-\-always
On conflict, overwrite the destination.
.TP
.BR \-N ", " \-\-never
On conflict, skip the source.
.TP
.BR \-\-conflict=\fIPOLICY\fR
One of
.BR fail ,
.BR overwrite ,
.BR rename ,
.BR skip
(default:
.BR fail ).
.B rename
chooses a unique name such as
.IR file\ (2).txt .
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
.TQ
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
.SH CONFLICT POLICIES
.TP
.B fail
Error and abort that item (default).
.TP
.B overwrite
Replace the existing destination.
.TP
.B rename
Unique name:
.IR stem\ (N).ext .
.TP
.B skip
Leave destination unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dirtoo (1),
.BR dt-move (1),
.BR dt-rename (1)
